export anchor BotanicalHerbariumStyle:
    number: 59
    screen: Calendar
    name: Botanical herbarium
    idea: Each day is a pressed-plant specimen sheet taped to parchment, its events written on small inked labels in a quiet museum hand.
    base: light
    palette:
        parchment: #efe8d4, the page background
        sheet: #fbf8ee, day sheets, the index panel, labels and the masthead
        ink: #2b2a1f, text, label borders, buttons and the selected view
        sepia: #635639, times, meta, Latin day names and sheet footers
        olive: #4b5626, the primary button, the today ring and the Team key
        oliveWash: #e3e5c8, the current week row and the focused field
        rust: #8a3b1e, Deadline labels and their pennant key
        slate: #4d5a63, Out of office labels and their crossed square key
        rule: #c7bb98, sheet edges and hairlines
        pencil: #b3aa86, the decorative plant drawings only
    type:
        Old style serif for almost everything, Iowan Old Style, Palatino
        Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, serif. Typewriter mono for
        times, eyebrows and sheet numbers, Courier New, Courier, monospace.
        Sizes are 34px regular for the week title with a 20px italic subtitle,
        22px regular day headings, 14px italic Latin day names, 15px semibold
        event titles, 13px mono times and 15px small caps section labels.
    layout:
        A thin masthead with a sprig mark, the wordmark in small caps, a text
        nav where the current item gets an ink underline and a fleuron, and a
        round double ring initials stamp for Mara. Below sit the eyebrow, the
        week title and the controls on one row. The week is a flowing grid of
        seven specimen sheets, about 210px minimum each, beside a 280px index
        panel on the right holding the month table, the calendar checkboxes
        and an out of office note. Each sheet has two strips of tape at the
        top, the day name and its Latin name, the event labels stacked, a
        faint pencil plant in the lower right and a footer reading Sheet 01
        and Coll. Brightwork. Below 1000px the index moves under the sheets,
        and below 640px the sheets stack in one column.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between sheets, 16 to 20px inside them, 10px between labels and 32px between areas.
    density: Airy. Seven sheets with at most two labels each, plenty of empty paper.
    corners: Square everywhere. Only the initials stamp and the today ring in the month are round.
    borders: 1px ink on labels and buttons, 1px rule on sheets. Deadlines use a 3px double rust rule and out of office a dashed slate rule. The today sheet gets an inset olive double line.
    shadows: One flat paper offset of 2px 3px with no blur in sepia at 12 percent. Translucent tan tape strips sit over the top edge.
    icons:
        Fine ink line icons at text size with a 1.4 stroke. A leaf marks Team,
        a pennant marks Deadline and a crossed square marks Out of office,
        always beside the word. Large pencil plant drawings decorate each
        sheet and carry no meaning.
    focus: A 2px dashed ink outline offset 3px. A focused field also gains the olive wash.
    tone: Calm and catalogue-like, such as Collected this week, Nothing scheduled and Sheet 04.
